{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish only the approved boot subtree on node1 as a read-only TFTP root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The TFTP service was rooted at the staged boot directory with read-only permissions and systemd confinement. Direct transfers succeeded, upload attempts failed, traversal outside the root failed, and the service remained available after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c274433f171476a","cmd-42b8270578e34ecf","cmd-c4f05e0f40b84e2e","cmd-2d301ded11c242ad"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to download boot.cfg and firmware.bin from node1 while preserving the approved bytes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 downloaded both files successfully. Their SHA-256 hashes matched the staged baseline, including firmware.bin, before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-551eb8c70d644d94","cmd-9aea6d1f02014bc9","cmd-2d301ded11c242ad","cmd-5d306a38669343c9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject TFTP uploads, including creation and overwrite attempts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A new-file upload and an overwrite attempt were both rejected, the unauthorized file was confirmed absent, and overwrite rejection was observed again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42b8270578e34ecf","cmd-4fc8466df05241a5","cmd-5d306a38669343c9"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Reject requests outside the published boot root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A path-as-is request for ../private/vendor-notes.txt was rejected without producing an output file, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42b8270578e34ecf","cmd-5d306a38669343c9"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The installed tftp-server package came from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2dc7214eae844782","cmd-c4f05e0f40b84e2e","cmd-5d306a38669343c9","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation was established: package installation, permissions and labeling, service configuration, firewall changes, diagnostic service restarts, temporary transfer files, and mandated node restarts all had evidence-supported roles; temporary client files were removed. The retained node2 firewall rule is a minor security-hygiene concern because it permits all UDP traffic from node1 to the full client ephemeral-port range, broader than TFTP reply traffic alone, although it directly enabled the required transfers. It remained configured after restart. No failed services, abandoned test files, or damaged package state were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2dc7214eae844782","cmd-8c274433f171476a","cmd-d1f34c487bd54bf7","cmd-52c7a310533d45d7","cmd-42b8270578e34ecf","cmd-5d306a38669343c9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct transfer, integrity, rejection, platform, and post-restart observations. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service and transfer behavior.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory firewall rules, installed packages, or service configuration, so those final-state details rely on direct executor command observations.","A new-file upload was tested before restart; the post-restart rejection test covered overwrite and outside-root access rather than repeating new-file creation."]}
